    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$4.02 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). Beans and sweet potatoes are cheap ballast, which is what lets a pot with this much pork shoulder in it land where it does.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eChipotles in adobo are the best flavor per dollar in the aisle.\u003c/strong\u003e One small can brings smoke and heat to the entire pot. Freeze the leftovers in a small bag and chip off what you need next time.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSweet potatoes are cheapest by the pound loose in fall.\u003c/strong\u003e They also thicken this chili naturally as they break down, so you are buying body and flavor in the same item.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePoblanos are milder and cheaper than bell peppers.\u003c/strong\u003e They bring a deeper roasted flavor for less money. If your store keeps them near the jalapenos, that is where the value hides.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eTwo cans of beans, two different kinds.\u003c/strong\u003e Black and kidney beans cost about the same and using both gives the chili more texture than a double dose of either."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cube the pork shoulder, pat it dry, season with salt, black pepper, chili powder, smoked paprika, ground cumin and a pinch of ground allspice, and brown it hard in the olive oil in batches.",
                    "Cook the diced onion and chopped poblano peppers in the same pot until soft, then add the minced garlic and the chopped chipotles in adobo and stir for a minute.",
                    "Stir in the Dijon mustard, the red wine vinegar and the splash of fish sauce, which sounds strange and is the reason this chili tastes like it cooked twice as long.",
                    "Add the diced tomatoes with their juice, return the pork, and simmer covered for about 2 hours until the pork shreds.",
                    "Add the cubed sweet potatoes and both drained beans and simmer another 30 minutes, until the sweet potato is tender and starting to break apart and thicken the pot.",
                    "Warm the tortillas and keep the sour cream and chopped cilantro in separate containers for topping at reheat."
                ],
